Z||000005||Formula88||06-23-2001||01:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bHooper:<BR><B>so do both of yall have your b-day on the same day?  if so that is to wierd... my college roomate and a my best friend have the  same birthday.<P>congrats!<P>hoop<P>p.s. <BR>trying to have blackie ready for tomorrow.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, it is weird.  Same birthday, and we both drive red '88 Formula 5-speeds!  But we're born on different years, so at least that's different (I'm the old one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>Hope to see you & blackie at Sonic tomorrow.  I've gotta fix an exhaust leak, re-bush my headlight motor, and install my Rodney 180 thermo and fan switch this afternoon.  It was my b-day, but the Fiero gets the presents!  Hopefully everything will be ready in time for tomorrow.<P>Later!<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000006||bHooper||06-23-2001||05:20 PM||||how peculiar... my friend and i have the exact same year, and color of GT... except that we are born on different years.<P>amazing isn't it?<P>i should be able to make sonic, as long as i get 5 chapters of N+ done between now and then.  <P>fun, isnt it?<P>(i've already done my exahust leak for the weekend... just make sure to put the dip stick in b4 you tilt the engine back, and dont touch any hot manifolds!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  )<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||06-23-2001||11:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bHooper:<BR><B>(i've already done my exahust leak for the weekend... just make sure to put the dip stick in b4 you tilt the engine back, and dont touch any hot manifolds!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  )<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, it's not my manifolds (knock on wood).  I had to cut my cat off cuz it plugged up, but since it had been replaced once before, the weld was right at the bend in the pipe.  So I'm having a hell of a time getting a seal between the new pipe and the old.  What I'm gonna have to do is replace the cat to muffler pipe, but I'm trying to patch this together long enough to get the West Coast Fiero hi-flow cat, Spin Tech muffler, and 2.5" exhaust pipeing they're making.  But all that together is more than I can afford right now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I've patched it a couple times, but it doesn't hold more than a few days.  There's just not enough straight pipe left to get a good seal on.<P>Hope to see you at the Sonic.  Anyone interested in catching The Fast and The Furious after lunch?||||reg||1
